No—people do not unknowingly pay $85 for a mint priced at $30 because the surplus is refunded.

The flow is:
User sends ~0.0145 ETH (~$45)
Contract swaps it into ~$44 USDC
Contract allocates $30 USDC to minting
Contract returns approximately ~$14 USDC to the user

This refund is already implemented in the contract at lines 820-832:
// Refund excess USDC if any
if (usdcReceived &gt; MINT\_PRICE) {
uint256 excess = usdcReceived - MINT\_PRICE;
require(usdc.transfer(msg.sender, excess), "Excess refund failed");
}
